b. Temporarily copying, building, and running the Covered Material on your own
   local computer, only to the extent reasonably necessary for that review;
c. Installing and running a finished program distributed by the copyright
   holder through an official channel such as the Chrome Web Store or GitHub
   Releases, solely as an individual end user.
d. Using GitHub's public-repository viewing and standard Fork features within
   the scope of GitHub's Terms of Service and Section 6.

Section 2 grants no other right to use, distribute, or reuse the Covered
Material.

3. Prohibited Activities

Without the copyright holder's prior written permission, you may not:

a. Copy any part of the Covered Material beyond the scope permitted by
   Section 2;
b. Modify, translate, adapt, or create derivative works based on the Covered
   Material;
c. Distribute, publish, post, relicense, sell, or resell the Covered Material
   or a derivative work;
d. Include or integrate any part of the Covered Material into a product,
   service, website, application, extension, library, dataset, or automated
   workflow;
e. Host the Covered Material or a derivative work, publicly or privately, or
   provide its functionality to a third party;
f. Operate a service for a third party using the Covered Material; or
g. Remove or alter copyright, license, or attribution notices.

4. Independent Implementations and Ideas

This license does not restrict ideas, principles, functions, or methods that
